    {
      "id": "b3_u07_l1_g2",
      "pattern": "A/V-(으)ㄹ 거예요 (taxmin)",
      "meaning_uz": "...sa kerak, ehtimol ... (taxmin)",
      "meaning_en": "Probably … (conjecture)",
      "explanation_md": "2-kitobda **-(으)ㄹ 거예요** reja edi (\"...aman\"). Boshqa odam yoki narsa haqida esa u **taxmin** bildiradi: \"**...sa kerak**\", \"**ehtimol ...**\".\n\n**아마 사람이 많을 거예요.** — *Ehtimol odam ko'p bo'ladi.*\n\n### Qanday yasaladi (2-kitobdagidek)\n\n- 받침siz → **-ㄹ 거예요**: 오다 → **올 거예요**, 친해지다 → **친해질 거예요**\n- 받침 bilan → **-을 거예요**: 많다 → **많을 거예요**, 괜찮다 → **괜찮을 거예요**\n- **ㅂ**: 어렵다 → **어려울 거예요**\n- O'tgan taxmin: **-았/었을 거예요**: 벌써 도착했을 거예요 — *Allaqachon yetib kelgan bo'lsa kerak.*\n\n### Ikki ma'noni farqlash\n\n- **저는 갈 거예요.** (men) — reja: *boraman.*\n- **민지 씨도 갈 거예요.** (boshqa odam) — taxmin: *Minji ham borsa kerak.*\n\n### Esda tuting\n\n- **아마** (ehtimol) bilan juda ko'p keladi.\n- Sifatlar bilan doim taxmin: **어색할 거예요** — *noqulay bo'lsa kerak.*",
      "explanation_md_en": "In book 2, **-(으)ㄹ 거예요** expressed a plan (\"I will\"). About other people or things it expresses a **guess**: \"**probably**\", \"**must be / will likely**\".\n\n**아마 사람이 많을 거예요.** — *There'll probably be lots of people.*\n\n### How to form it (as in book 2)\n\n- No 받침 → **-ㄹ 거예요**: 오다 → **올 거예요**, 친해지다 → **친해질 거예요**\n- With 받침 → **-을 거예요**: 많다 → **많을 거예요**, 괜찮다 → **괜찮을 거예요**\n- **ㅂ**: 어렵다 → **어려울 거예요**\n- Past guess: **-았/었을 거예요**: 벌써 도착했을 거예요 — *They've probably arrived already.*\n\n### Telling the two apart\n\n- **저는 갈 거예요.** (I) — plan: *I'll go.*\n- **민지 씨도 갈 거예요.** (someone else) — guess: *Minji will probably go too.*\n\n### Remember\n\n- It often pairs with **아마** (probably).\n- With adjectives it's always a guess: **어색할 거예요** — *it'll probably be awkward.*",
      "formation": [
